1
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:13,000
Guess I’ll play dumb.

2
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:14,000
That’s right.

3
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:16,000
He seems to like Gon,

4
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:18,000
so he might help us.

5
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:20,000
-[Gon] Hey!
-[Killua] You idiot!

6
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:24,000
Oh, yeah! Oops…

7
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:26,000
What?

8
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:27,000
Do you know someone here?

9
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:30,000
Uh… no…

10
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:33,000
Hey!

11
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:34,000
It’s that girl we met!

12
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:37,000
[Phinks] Is that true, Shizuku?
You know these guys?

13
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:39,000
No. I sure don’t.

14
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:40,000
[Killua] Huh?

15
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:43,000
[Feitan] Oh… I remember now.

16
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:45,000
The kid who arm wrestles.

17
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:47,000
Refresh my memory.

18
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:48,000
That kid.

19
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:51,000
You lost to him
in an arm-wrestling contest two days ago.

20
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:53,000
I did? He beat me?

21
00:00:53,000 --> 00:00:54,000
That’s a lie!

22
00:00:54,000 --> 00:00:57,000
I’m not the strongest,
but I wouldn’t lose to a kid…

23
00:00:57,000 --> 00:00:58,000
Well...

24
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:01,000
It’s because you were using
your right hand.

25
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:03,000
I did? But why? I’m left handed.

26
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:04,000
[Feitan] Don't bother.

27
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:08,000
Once she has forgotten something,
it is gone for good.

28
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:11,000
Right. Never mind, guess I was mistaken.

29
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:12,000
Thought so.

30
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:14,000
Hold on. Is that right?

31
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:16,000
You really beat Shizuku?

32
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:17,000
Yeah.

33
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:20,000
I never would have imagined
that she was a Phantom Troupe member.

34
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:24,000
Okay. Then show me what you’ve got.

35
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:33,000
[theme song playing]

36
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:49,000
ALLY x AND x SWORD

37
00:02:51,000 --> 00:02:52,000
[Nobunaga] One more time.

38
00:02:56,000 --> 00:02:57,000
Ready…

39
00:02:58,000 --> 00:02:59,000
Go.

40
00:02:59,000 --> 00:03:01,000
[straining]

41
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:13,000
All right, one more time.

42
00:03:17,000 --> 00:03:18,000
Ready…

43
00:03:19,000 --> 00:03:20,000
Go.

44
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:22,000
[straining]

45
00:03:25,000 --> 00:03:26,000
So...

46
00:03:27,000 --> 00:03:30,000
How do I stack up
against all the other Spiders?

47
00:03:30,000 --> 00:03:31,000
Be honest.

48
00:03:32,000 --> 00:03:35,000
Probably seventh or eighth, I’d guess.

49
00:03:35,000 --> 00:03:38,000
Well you aren’t the weakest
but not the strongest, either.

50
00:03:39,000 --> 00:03:40,000
Right.

51
00:03:40,000 --> 00:03:43,000
The strongest member of the Troupe
was this guy called Uvogin.

52
00:03:44,000 --> 00:03:47,000
But it’s starting to look like
the chain user killed him.

53
00:03:47,000 --> 00:03:50,000
We told you!
We have no clue who that is!

54
00:03:50,000 --> 00:03:51,000
[Nobunaga] Hey, kid!

55
00:03:53,000 --> 00:03:55,000
Speak without my permission again…

56
00:03:57,000 --> 00:03:58,000
and I’ll kill you.

57
00:04:02,000 --> 00:04:04,000
Now, one more time.

58
00:04:05,000 --> 00:04:06,000
Ready…

59
00:04:07,000 --> 00:04:08,000
Go.

60
00:04:11,000 --> 00:04:13,000
Uvogin was an Enhancer.

61
00:04:14,000 --> 00:04:18,000
He was simple-minded, straightforward,
and he loved a good fight.

62
00:04:18,000 --> 00:04:19,000
And punctual.

63
00:04:20,000 --> 00:04:21,000
A real stickler about time.

64
00:04:21,000 --> 00:04:23,000
Whenever Franklin or I were late,

65
00:04:23,000 --> 00:04:25,000
he’d always start something.

66
00:04:27,000 --> 00:04:29,000
He beat the crap out of me
more than once, I can tell ya!

67
00:04:31,000 --> 00:04:34,000
I’ve known him since
before the Troupe was founded.

68
00:04:34,000 --> 00:04:36,000
I know him better than anyone.

69
00:04:38,000 --> 00:04:39,000
He would never...

70
00:04:40,000 --> 00:04:41,000
I mean never

71
00:04:41,000 --> 00:04:44,000
lose in a fair fight, do you hear me?

72
00:04:44,000 --> 00:04:47,000
Not unless he was caught
in some dirty trap!

73
00:04:49,000 --> 00:04:51,000
I’ll make his killer pay.

74
00:04:52,000 --> 00:04:56,000
I’ll find him,
no matter who I have to kill.

75
00:04:57,000 --> 00:05:00,000
The chain user holds
some kind of grudge against us -

76
00:05:00,000 --> 00:05:01,000
a strong one.

77
00:05:01,000 --> 00:05:04,000
The Mafia’s Nostrade family
hired him recently.

78
00:05:05,000 --> 00:05:07,000
[Killua] A grudge against the Troupe…

79
00:05:07,000 --> 00:05:09,000
A recent hire? [gasps]

80
00:05:10,000 --> 00:05:11,000
You may not know him personally

81
00:05:11,000 --> 00:05:13,000
but maybe you heard rumors…

82
00:05:14,000 --> 00:05:15,000
So, think hard, all right?

83
00:05:15,000 --> 00:05:18,000
You’d better not hold anything back!

84
00:05:19,000 --> 00:05:20,000
I don’t know him.

85
00:05:21,000 --> 00:05:22,000
But even if I did,

86
00:05:22,000 --> 00:05:24,000
I would still never give him up to you!

87
00:05:25,000 --> 00:05:28,000
I thought you were all
a bunch of cold-blooded monsters

88
00:05:29,000 --> 00:05:31,000
but I see you can shed tears
for your friends.

89
00:05:34,000 --> 00:05:36,000
So, you’re capable of empathy.

90
00:05:36,000 --> 00:05:37,000
But you’ve killed...

91
00:05:38,000 --> 00:05:39,000
you’ve killed so many people!

92
00:05:40,000 --> 00:05:42,000
Why couldn’t you feel that for them?

93
00:05:42,000 --> 00:05:43,000
[yells] What the hell is wrong with you?!

94
00:05:51,000 --> 00:05:52,000
[seething]

95
00:05:54,000 --> 00:05:56,000
Careful. You’re too cocky.

96
00:05:57,000 --> 00:05:58,000
[grunt of pain]

97
00:05:58,000 --> 00:05:59,000
Gon!

98
00:06:07,000 --> 00:06:09,000
Move and I’ll cut you.

99
00:06:09,000 --> 00:06:11,000
[Feitan] Answer the question.

100
00:06:11,000 --> 00:06:14,000
Do you know who the chain user is?

101
00:06:14,000 --> 00:06:15,000
I told you!

102
00:06:16,000 --> 00:06:18,000
I’m not telling you anything,
so get off me!

103
00:06:18,000 --> 00:06:20,000
[Feitan smirks]

104
00:06:21,000 --> 00:06:22,000
[Nobunaga] Feitan.

105
00:06:23,000 --> 00:06:24,000
Stop it.

106
00:06:25,000 --> 00:06:26,000
[Feitan] Stop what?

107
00:06:27,000 --> 00:06:29,000
Stop doing what you’re just about to do.

108
00:06:29,000 --> 00:06:33,000
[Feitan] Oh? You think you know
what I’m about to do?

109
00:06:33,000 --> 00:06:35,000
You’re going to break his arm, aren’t you?

110
00:06:35,000 --> 00:06:37,000
I’d start with a finger…

111
00:06:38,000 --> 00:06:39,000
peel off a nail.

112
00:06:40,000 --> 00:06:41,000
Doesn’t matter.

113
00:06:41,000 --> 00:06:43,000
I told you to stop it!

114
00:06:43,000 --> 00:06:45,000
You’re giving me orders?

115
00:06:45,000 --> 00:06:47,000
I don’t have to obey.

116
00:06:56,000 --> 00:06:59,000
Hey, quit it, Nobunaga.

117
00:06:59,000 --> 00:07:02,000
What, have you
already forgotten the rules?

118
00:07:02,000 --> 00:07:05,000
There’s no physical fighting
between the Troupe members.

119
00:07:05,000 --> 00:07:07,000
I know, I know.

120
00:07:07,000 --> 00:07:09,000
Disputes are decided by a coin toss.

121
00:07:13,000 --> 00:07:15,000
[Feitan] Tails.

122
00:07:15,000 --> 00:07:16,000
[Nobunaga] Then I’m heads.

123
00:07:21,000 --> 00:07:22,000
It’s heads.

124
00:07:22,000 --> 00:07:23,000
So, let him go.

125
00:07:28,000 --> 00:07:29,000
[Shizuku] Well, what do we do with them?

126
00:07:30,000 --> 00:07:33,000
They haven’t told us
anything about the chain user.

127
00:07:33,000 --> 00:07:36,000
If they don’t know anything,
then just let ‘em go.

128
00:07:37,000 --> 00:07:38,000
Am I right, Pakunoda?

129
00:07:39,000 --> 00:07:40,000
[Pakunoda] I checked on the trip here.

130
00:07:41,000 --> 00:07:42,000
It’s true.

131
00:07:43,000 --> 00:07:45,000
They really don’t know anything.

132
00:07:46,000 --> 00:07:47,000
-[Machi] You sure?
-I am.

133
00:07:48,000 --> 00:07:51,000
They have no memories
of the chain user whatsoever.

134
00:07:52,000 --> 00:07:55,000
Looks like your hunch
was a little off this time, huh?

135
00:07:55,000 --> 00:07:56,000
That’s bizarre…

136
00:07:56,000 --> 00:08:00,000
Oh well. If Pakunoda says so,
it must be true.

137
00:08:11,000 --> 00:08:12,000
Hey, Gon.

138
00:08:12,000 --> 00:08:14,000
Did they do anything to you
on the way here?

139
00:08:14,000 --> 00:08:17,000
Not really. Just asked me some questions.

140
00:08:17,000 --> 00:08:18,000
Thought so.

141
00:08:19,000 --> 00:08:21,000
[Killua] So she examined us
without us knowing.

142
00:08:22,000 --> 00:08:23,000
What was it?

143
00:08:23,000 --> 00:08:24,000
And how?

144
00:08:25,000 --> 00:08:27,000
It sounds like
they all have a lot of faith

145
00:08:27,000 --> 00:08:29,000
in that Pakunoda woman’s
judgment.

146
00:08:31,000 --> 00:08:33,000
Her skill must be
more accurate than instinct.

147
00:08:35,000 --> 00:08:38,000
[Pakunoda] They have no memories
of the chain user whatsoever.

148
00:08:38,000 --> 00:08:39,000
[Killua] Memories?

149
00:08:40,000 --> 00:08:41,000
How about you?

150
00:08:42,000 --> 00:08:43,000
Have any guesses?

151
00:08:43,000 --> 00:08:45,000
[Killua] The power
to scan someone’s memory!

152
00:08:46,000 --> 00:08:47,000
By what, touching them?

153
00:08:48,000 --> 00:08:50,000
That would explain everything.

154
00:08:50,000 --> 00:08:52,000
We’re in big trouble.

155
00:08:53,000 --> 00:08:55,000
When she scanned us before,

156
00:08:55,000 --> 00:08:57,000
I had no idea who the chain user was.

157
00:08:58,000 --> 00:08:59,000
But now…

158
00:08:59,000 --> 00:09:00,000
I have an image in my head.

159
00:09:02,000 --> 00:09:04,000
If she checks again...

160
00:09:05,000 --> 00:09:07,000
[Franklin] They don’t know the chain user.

161
00:09:07,000 --> 00:09:09,000
so can’t we just let them go now?

162
00:09:09,000 --> 00:09:12,000
[Shalnark] Yeah. I really don’t see
the point in keeping them here.

163
00:09:13,000 --> 00:09:16,000
[Phinks] No. We can’t be sure
they’re completely unrelated.

164
00:09:16,000 --> 00:09:18,000
It’s possible they’re being used.

165
00:09:19,000 --> 00:09:21,000
The chain user is discreet.

166
00:09:21,000 --> 00:09:23,000
He usually keeps his chains hidden.

167
00:09:23,000 --> 00:09:25,000
If that’s the case,

168
00:09:25,000 --> 00:09:27,000
maybe they don’t realize he’s
who we’re talking about.

169
00:09:28,000 --> 00:09:29,000
We shouldn’t release them.

170
00:09:30,000 --> 00:09:32,000
Not until they tell us
who they’re working for.

171
00:09:32,000 --> 00:09:34,000
If they are working for someone,

172
00:09:34,000 --> 00:09:36,000
then it isn’t the chain user.

173
00:09:36,000 --> 00:09:38,000
Because he prefers
to operate all by himself.

174
00:09:39,000 --> 00:09:41,000
[Machi] So, you’re saying
you agree with Nobunaga?

175
00:09:42,000 --> 00:09:45,000
We can get whatever information we need
from the Nostrade family.

176
00:09:45,000 --> 00:09:47,000
We don’t really need these kids for that.

177
00:09:48,000 --> 00:09:49,000
After all…

178
00:09:49,000 --> 00:09:51,000
we know the chain user is a member.

179
00:09:52,000 --> 00:09:53,000
That’s right, we do.

180
00:09:54,000 --> 00:09:56,000
Our only target right now
is the chain user,

181
00:09:57,000 --> 00:09:59,000
so we can pretty much ignore
everybody else.

182
00:10:00,000 --> 00:10:01,000
[Feitan] There you go.

183
00:10:01,000 --> 00:10:02,000
You are lucky.

184
00:10:04,000 --> 00:10:05,000
[Nobunaga] Not just yet.

185
00:10:08,000 --> 00:10:10,000
I’m not letting the kid go.

186
00:10:11,000 --> 00:10:13,000
You wanna join the Spiders?

187
00:10:15,000 --> 00:10:16,000
Team up with me.

188
00:10:17,000 --> 00:10:18,000
No.

189
00:10:18,000 --> 00:10:20,000
I would rather die
than team up with you guys!

190
00:10:20,000 --> 00:10:22,000
So, it’s never gonna happen!

191
00:10:22,000 --> 00:10:24,000
[laughing]

192
00:10:24,000 --> 00:10:26,000
He really hates us, doesn’t he?

193
00:10:26,000 --> 00:10:28,000
What are you?
You’re an Enhancer, right?

194
00:10:29,000 --> 00:10:30,000
Yeah, and what if I am?

195
00:10:31,000 --> 00:10:32,000
I thought you’d say that.

196
00:10:32,000 --> 00:10:33,000
[chuckling]

197
00:10:34,000 --> 00:10:36,000
[laughter]

198
00:10:39,000 --> 00:10:40,000
[Nobunaga] Hey!

199
00:10:40,000 --> 00:10:43,000
We’re keeping them here
until the Boss gets back.

200
00:10:44,000 --> 00:10:45,000
I’m nominating him.

201
00:10:46,000 --> 00:10:47,000
Are you serious?

202
00:10:47,000 --> 00:10:50,000
[Feitan] The Boss will never agree
to that.

203
00:10:51,000 --> 00:10:52,000
[Machi] Fine, whatever.

204
00:10:53,000 --> 00:10:54,000
But you’ve gotta babysit ‘em.

205
00:10:55,000 --> 00:10:57,000
It’s on you if they escape.

206
00:11:02,000 --> 00:11:04,000
[Shizuku] Really? He reminds you of Uvo?

207
00:11:05,000 --> 00:11:08,000
Yeah. He wears all his emotions
right on his sleeve.

208
00:11:08,000 --> 00:11:10,000
And when he’s mad,
he forgets about the consequences.

209
00:11:11,000 --> 00:11:13,000
But what’s the most like Uvo,

210
00:11:13,000 --> 00:11:16,000
is he’s at his absolute strongest
when he’s fighting for someone else.

211
00:11:17,000 --> 00:11:19,000
He liked to fight alone

212
00:11:19,000 --> 00:11:21,000
but Uvo was never more powerful

213
00:11:21,000 --> 00:11:23,000
than when he would go off
and team up with Nobunaga

214
00:11:24,000 --> 00:11:25,000
to fight an entire horde.

215
00:11:26,000 --> 00:11:27,000
He never admitted it,

216
00:11:28,000 --> 00:11:31,000
but I think Uvo preferred
having someone there to protect.

217
00:11:32,000 --> 00:11:34,000
[Shizuku] He was stronger
when someone was holding him back?

218
00:11:34,000 --> 00:11:36,000
[Franklin] I guess you could say that…

219
00:11:37,000 --> 00:11:39,000
[Feitan] She does not mince words,
does she?

220
00:11:39,000 --> 00:11:40,000
On the other hand,

221
00:11:40,000 --> 00:11:43,000
Nobunaga’s skills
are excellent for dueling.

222
00:11:43,000 --> 00:11:46,000
You might even say
that they’re only effective one-on-one.

223
00:11:47,000 --> 00:11:51,000
Whenever those two had to fight together,
they would always complain.

224
00:11:51,000 --> 00:11:53,000
But I’m pretty sure they both enjoyed it.

225
00:11:54,000 --> 00:11:55,000
[Shalnark] Okay. Enough reminiscing.

226
00:11:56,000 --> 00:11:57,000
Let’s get down to business.

227
00:11:58,000 --> 00:12:00,000
Here’s a full list
of the Nostrade family members.

228
00:12:00,000 --> 00:12:03,000
I got it straight
from the official Hunter website.

229
00:12:04,000 --> 00:12:05,000
These five are especially important.

230
00:12:06,000 --> 00:12:09,000
They serve as full time bodyguards
for the Boss’s daughter.

231
00:12:09,000 --> 00:12:12,000
Not to mention the fact
that they’re the ones who captured Uvo.

232
00:12:13,000 --> 00:12:16,000
But Uvo was certain
that the chain user wasn’t on this list.

233
00:12:16,000 --> 00:12:19,000
And since we have no idea
what he looks like,

234
00:12:19,000 --> 00:12:21,000
we’re going to need
to find someone who does.

235
00:12:22,000 --> 00:12:24,000
Hey. That’s the guy I killed.

236
00:12:24,000 --> 00:12:26,000
The one on the top left.
You can cross him off.

237
00:12:26,000 --> 00:12:28,000
[Shalnark] All right pair up
and search the area.

238
00:12:29,000 --> 00:12:30,000
And keep a sharp eye out

239
00:12:30,000 --> 00:12:32,000
for any of the people
that are on this list.

240
00:12:33,000 --> 00:12:35,000
We’ll all meet back here at ten p.m.

241
00:12:35,000 --> 00:12:36,000
Got it? Let’s move.

242
00:12:38,000 --> 00:12:39,000
[Machi] Hey, hold on!

243
00:12:39,000 --> 00:12:41,000
Nobunaga’s staying here, right?

244
00:12:41,000 --> 00:12:42,000
What about me?

245
00:12:43,000 --> 00:12:45,000
You can just team up with whoever is left.

246
00:12:48,000 --> 00:12:49,000
[light chuckle]

247
00:12:52,000 --> 00:12:53,000
[resigned sigh]

248
00:12:58,000 --> 00:12:59,000
Ow…

249
00:13:00,000 --> 00:13:02,000
[Killua] That was stupid of me…

250
00:13:02,000 --> 00:13:03,000
If I’d made a move,

251
00:13:03,000 --> 00:13:06,000
Hisoka would’ve killed me
without a second thought.

252
00:13:07,000 --> 00:13:09,000
That murderous aura…

253
00:13:09,000 --> 00:13:10,000
I was paralyzed.

254
00:13:11,000 --> 00:13:13,000
If they’d threatened to kill Gon,

255
00:13:13,000 --> 00:13:14,000
would I have been able to stop them?

256
00:13:15,000 --> 00:13:17,000
Would I have even been able to move?

257
00:13:18,000 --> 00:13:19,000
[Illumi] You can’t do it, can you?

258
00:13:20,000 --> 00:13:22,000
Because deep down inside,

259
00:13:22,000 --> 00:13:23,000
you’re more worried about

260
00:13:24,000 --> 00:13:26,000
whether you can defeat me
than anything else.

261
00:13:26,000 --> 00:13:27,000
[Killua] You’re wrong!!

262
00:13:27,000 --> 00:13:30,000
Remember the lesson I drilled into you?

263
00:13:30,000 --> 00:13:33,000
Never go up against a superior opponent.

264
00:13:33,000 --> 00:13:35,000
No, you’re wrong!

265
00:13:40,000 --> 00:13:42,000
[scoffs] Pretty scary.

266
00:13:43,000 --> 00:13:45,000
If looks could kill, huh?

267
00:13:47,000 --> 00:13:48,000
I should warn you…

268
00:13:49,000 --> 00:13:52,000
Step into range and I’ll cut you down.

269
00:13:54,000 --> 00:13:55,000
Killua!

270
00:14:09,000 --> 00:14:11,000
[Killua - shallow breathing]

271
00:14:30,000 --> 00:14:32,000
[Killua] I don’t stand a chance
against him.

272
00:14:33,000 --> 00:14:35,000
I’ve gotta think of a way to escape…

273
00:14:36,000 --> 00:14:37,000
No windows…

274
00:14:38,000 --> 00:14:40,000
and only one exit.

275
00:14:40,000 --> 00:14:44,000
How are we supposed to get him
to move away from the door?

276
00:14:48,000 --> 00:14:51,000
Hey, I wonder if Leorio is okay.

277
00:14:51,000 --> 00:14:54,000
I really hope he was able
to get a hold of Mister Zepile…

278
00:14:56,000 --> 00:14:57,000
Killua? You okay?

279
00:14:58,000 --> 00:14:59,000
Yeah.

280
00:15:05,000 --> 00:15:06,000
Let’s see……

281
00:15:06,000 --> 00:15:11,000
Mister Zepile taught us cauterization,
autopsy and something else.

282
00:15:11,000 --> 00:15:12,000
Remember what it was?

283
00:15:13,000 --> 00:15:14,000
I forgot.

284
00:15:14,000 --> 00:15:16,000
Was it osmosis, maybe?

285
00:15:17,000 --> 00:15:19,000
I don’t think it was,
but I just don’t know…

286
00:15:19,000 --> 00:15:20,000
[Killua] Gon.

287
00:15:22,000 --> 00:15:23,000
I’ll be the decoy.

288
00:15:23,000 --> 00:15:24,000
Wait for it

289
00:15:25,000 --> 00:15:26,000
and then try to escape.

290
00:15:27,000 --> 00:15:29,000
What are you talking about?

291
00:15:29,000 --> 00:15:30,000
[Nobunaga] Look, seriously…

292
00:15:31,000 --> 00:15:32,000
forget all about it.

293
00:15:32,000 --> 00:15:36,000
You’re good enough to recognize
the difference in our abilities.

294
00:15:37,000 --> 00:15:38,000
You won’t catch me off guard.

295
00:15:39,000 --> 00:15:40,000
I know that already!

296
00:15:42,000 --> 00:15:44,000
This room has one exit
and nowhere to hide.

297
00:15:45,000 --> 00:15:47,000
He can see everything we’re doing.

298
00:15:47,000 --> 00:15:50,000
He can even keep an eye on us
without ever creating an opening.

299
00:15:52,000 --> 00:15:54,000
He’s probably an Iaido master,

300
00:15:54,000 --> 00:15:55,000
and with his shodachi,

301
00:15:55,000 --> 00:15:57,000
his range is twice mine.

302
00:15:58,000 --> 00:15:59,000
One step too close

303
00:15:59,000 --> 00:16:01,000
and I’m dead meat.

304
00:16:02,000 --> 00:16:03,000
But that’s what gives it meaning!

305
00:16:04,000 --> 00:16:06,000
[Illumi] You can’t do it, can you?

306
00:16:07,000 --> 00:16:08,000
Shut up, all right?!

307
00:16:09,000 --> 00:16:11,000
The only way I’ll find out is if I try!

308
00:16:14,000 --> 00:16:17,000
Killua, what are you thinking about doing?

309
00:16:17,000 --> 00:16:20,000
[Killua] I’ll stop his shodachi,
even if it kills me.

310
00:16:20,000 --> 00:16:21,000
When I do,

311
00:16:21,000 --> 00:16:22,000
you run away!

312
00:16:24,000 --> 00:16:25,000
[Gon angered grunt]

313
00:16:25,000 --> 00:16:26,000
Huh?

314
00:16:26,000 --> 00:16:28,000
[yells] What the hell was that for, huh?!

315
00:16:28,000 --> 00:16:30,000
-Stop being so selfish!
-Huh?

316
00:16:31,000 --> 00:16:33,000
Don’t talk about dying
like it’s no big deal?!

317
00:16:33,000 --> 00:16:37,000
Why not? You did!
You said the same thing earlier!

318
00:16:37,000 --> 00:16:38,000
I’m allowed to!

319
00:16:38,000 --> 00:16:40,000
But you’re not, do you hear me?!

320
00:16:40,000 --> 00:16:41,000
Huh?

321
00:16:42,000 --> 00:16:43,000
[Nobunaga laughing]

322
00:16:43,000 --> 00:16:45,000
Reason never works on an Enhancer.

323
00:16:46,000 --> 00:16:47,000
I thought you knew that, kid!

324
00:16:48,000 --> 00:16:50,000
We can’t escape
unless we’re prepared to die,

325
00:16:50,000 --> 00:16:51,000
you stupid little jerk!

326
00:16:51,000 --> 00:16:53,000
You don’t know what I was thinking!

327
00:16:53,000 --> 00:16:55,000
So, tell me, who’s the selfish one now?!

328
00:16:55,000 --> 00:16:58,000
No! I don’t know!
‘Cause I’m stupid!

329
00:16:58,000 --> 00:17:00,000
[hearty laughter]

330
00:17:00,000 --> 00:17:02,000
You two kids are hilarious, you know that?

331
00:17:03,000 --> 00:17:05,000
Listen I’m not gonna hurt you.

332
00:17:05,000 --> 00:17:06,000
Just behave yourselves.

333
00:17:07,000 --> 00:17:09,000
I know you guys mean business, all right?

334
00:17:09,000 --> 00:17:11,000
Don’t throw your lives away.

335
00:17:12,000 --> 00:17:14,000
Sit tight and wait
until the Boss gets back.

336
00:17:15,000 --> 00:17:16,000
And if you don’t strike his fancy,

337
00:17:16,000 --> 00:17:18,000
you get to leave, free and clear.

338
00:17:20,000 --> 00:17:22,000
But try to escape and I’ll kill you.

339
00:17:22,000 --> 00:17:25,000
Make me draw my sword from its scabbard

340
00:17:25,000 --> 00:17:27,000
and you won’t survive to talk about it.

341
00:17:29,000 --> 00:17:30,000
[Gon] Oh!

342
00:17:30,000 --> 00:17:32,000
I remember now!

343
00:17:32,000 --> 00:17:33,000
The other one is ostomy!

344
00:17:34,000 --> 00:17:35,000
Cauterization, autopsy…

345
00:17:36,000 --> 00:17:38,000
and the last one’s ostomy!

346
00:17:41,000 --> 00:17:43,000
Do you remember now?

347
00:17:43,000 --> 00:17:45,000
Yeah! I just wish
I’d thought of it sooner!

348
00:17:45,000 --> 00:17:46,000
Right?

349
00:17:46,000 --> 00:17:49,000
I can’t believe we both
forgot something so simple!

350
00:17:49,000 --> 00:17:50,000
What?

351
00:17:52,000 --> 00:17:53,000
Now that we’ve figured that out…

352
00:17:54,000 --> 00:17:55,000
Let's go!

353
00:17:55,000 --> 00:17:57,000
Are you serious?

354
00:17:57,000 --> 00:17:59,000
You know you’re going to die.

355
00:17:59,000 --> 00:18:02,000
I’m not nearly skilled or merciful enough

356
00:18:02,000 --> 00:18:04,000
to temper my strength to face you.

357
00:18:07,000 --> 00:18:08,000
You fools!

358
00:18:13,000 --> 00:18:15,000
[Gon] If the exit is blocked…

359
00:18:16,000 --> 00:18:18,000
[Killua] ...you’ve just gotta
make your own!

360
00:18:19,000 --> 00:18:20,000
[Nobunaga] The wall…

361
00:18:21,000 --> 00:18:23,000
Which one do I chase?

362
00:18:23,000 --> 00:18:25,000
We’re on the fifth floor.

363
00:18:25,000 --> 00:18:27,000
The cat-eyed kid’s already by the stairs.

364
00:18:28,000 --> 00:18:29,000
So, the black-haired kid!

365
00:18:31,000 --> 00:18:34,000
There. Now he doesn’t have
anywhere to run.

366
00:18:36,000 --> 00:18:37,000
What am I thinking?

367
00:18:37,000 --> 00:18:40,000
They can keep
breaking through walls to escape!

368
00:18:43,000 --> 00:18:44,000
The cat-eyed kid is below.

369
00:18:44,000 --> 00:18:47,000
I’ll stay on the black-haired one.

370
00:18:50,000 --> 00:18:51,000
Where is he?

371
00:18:52,000 --> 00:18:53,000
The walls are intact.

372
00:18:53,000 --> 00:18:55,000
So’s the door.

373
00:18:55,000 --> 00:18:57,000
Killua! Are you there?

374
00:18:58,000 --> 00:19:00,000
[Killua] Yeah! I’m here!

375
00:19:01,000 --> 00:19:02,000
That’s it!

376
00:19:02,000 --> 00:19:04,000
Then that must mean the last hole…

377
00:19:05,000 --> 00:19:06,000
was a decoy!

378
00:19:06,000 --> 00:19:08,000
He busted the wall,

379
00:19:08,000 --> 00:19:11,000
then doubled back and hid
in the next room, so I’d pass him!

380
00:19:13,000 --> 00:19:15,000
We can beat him. The two of us!

381
00:19:20,000 --> 00:19:21,000
His presence disappeared.

382
00:19:21,000 --> 00:19:22,000
Zetsu?

383
00:19:23,000 --> 00:19:26,000
Does this idiot really want to fight me?

384
00:19:27,000 --> 00:19:30,000
An advanced application of Ten and Ren…

385
00:19:32,000 --> 00:19:33,000
En!

386
00:19:34,000 --> 00:19:35,000
Aura envelops the body

387
00:19:36,000 --> 00:19:39,000
in a layer a few millimeters
to a couple centimeters thick.

388
00:19:39,000 --> 00:19:42,000
But with En, you can extend it
as far as necessary.

389
00:19:43,000 --> 00:19:45,000
You can sense anyone who enters your En.

390
00:19:46,000 --> 00:19:49,000
Inside it you can even count the leaves
as they fall.

391
00:19:51,000 --> 00:19:54,000
You can conceal your presence
before your approach,

392
00:19:54,000 --> 00:19:56,000
never making a sound.

393
00:19:57,000 --> 00:20:00,000
But enter my En and my sword flies.

394
00:20:01,000 --> 00:20:02,000
Come. I’m ready.

395
00:20:05,000 --> 00:20:06,000
[Killua] That idiot.

396
00:20:06,000 --> 00:20:09,000
Man. I really wanted to beat that guy up.

397
00:20:09,000 --> 00:20:10,000
Yeah, fat chance of that.

398
00:20:11,000 --> 00:20:13,000
He’d kill you twice before you tried.

399
00:20:13,000 --> 00:20:14,000
[Gon] You sure about that?

400
00:20:15,000 --> 00:20:17,000
[Killua] We only know the basics of Nen.

401
00:20:17,000 --> 00:20:19,000
We wouldn’t stand a chance.

402
00:20:19,000 --> 00:20:20,000
[chuckles]

403
00:20:20,000 --> 00:20:22,000
What’s so funny?

404
00:20:22,000 --> 00:20:24,000
You’re back to being your old self again!

405
00:20:24,000 --> 00:20:26,000
It’s my job to be reckless…

406
00:20:26,000 --> 00:20:29,000
and it’s your job to stay cool
and keep me in line!

407
00:20:29,000 --> 00:20:30,000
[light derisive snort]

408
00:20:30,000 --> 00:20:32,000
Glad I can count on ya, pal!

409
00:20:32,000 --> 00:20:33,000
You’re being selfish!

410
00:20:34,000 --> 00:20:36,000
[Gon] Well? What do we do next?

411
00:20:37,000 --> 00:20:39,000
[Killua] Depends on what
we wanna do, I guess.

412
00:20:39,000 --> 00:20:41,000
Okay. I wanna kick their butts!

413
00:20:41,000 --> 00:20:42,000
Figured.

414
00:20:42,000 --> 00:20:45,000
Well, that’s not too different
from the original plan.

415
00:20:46,000 --> 00:20:48,000
But both of us’ll need to improve our Nen,

416
00:20:48,000 --> 00:20:50,000
if that’s what we decide we’re gonna do.

417
00:20:50,000 --> 00:20:53,000
There’s only one way we might get
as strong as we’ll need to

418
00:20:54,000 --> 00:20:55,000
and that’s Nen.

419
00:20:57,000 --> 00:20:58,000
And the fastest way

420
00:20:59,000 --> 00:21:00,000
is through Kurapika.

421
00:21:00,000 --> 00:21:01,000
We need to go ask him.

422
00:21:02,000 --> 00:21:03,000
[Gon] Huh? Why?

423
00:21:03,000 --> 00:21:06,000
[Killua] Because he’s the “chain user”
who defeated their friend

424
00:21:06,000 --> 00:21:08,000
and got us into this mess.

425
00:21:08,000 --> 00:21:09,000
[Gon] What?

426
00:21:09,000 --> 00:21:11,000
[Killua] Wait, you hadn’t figured
that out yet?

427
00:21:11,000 --> 00:21:12,000
[Gon] You really think it’s Kurapika?

428
00:21:13,000 --> 00:21:14,000
I’m pretty sure it is.

429
00:21:15,000 --> 00:21:16,000
And if I’m right,

430
00:21:16,000 --> 00:21:17,000
we still have a chance.

431
00:21:18,000 --> 00:21:21,000
You and I both started learning Nen
at around the same time Kurapika did.

432
00:21:22,000 --> 00:21:23,000
What we need to do now

433
00:21:23,000 --> 00:21:25,000
is learn the unique abilities
that fit our talents.

434
00:21:26,000 --> 00:21:28,000
But what’s even more important…

435
00:21:28,000 --> 00:21:31,000
we’ve got to gain the strength
we’ll need to face the Phantom Troupe.

436
00:21:31,000 --> 00:21:35,000
And you really think Kurapika’s the key
to finding the answers we’re looking for?

437
00:21:35,000 --> 00:21:36,000
Yeah.

438
00:21:42,000 --> 00:21:45,000
[narrator] Meanwhile, deep in
the troubled heart of Yorknew City

439
00:21:45,000 --> 00:21:48,000
a fearsome storm has begun to brew.

440
00:21:49,000 --> 00:21:52,000
[theme song playing]

441
00:22:58,000 --> 00:22:59,000
[Gon] Coming up:

442
00:22:59,000 --> 00:23:00,000
-Gon...
-[Killua] ...and Killua’s…

443
00:23:00,000 --> 00:23:02,000
[both] Hunterpedia!

444
00:23:02,000 --> 00:23:03,000
-I’m Gon!
-I’m Killua!

445
00:23:04,000 --> 00:23:05,000
[both] And this is our Hunterpedia!

446
00:23:05,000 --> 00:23:07,000
Today, we’ll introduce Franklin.

447
00:23:07,000 --> 00:23:09,000
He’s an Emitter
and a Phantom Troupe member!

448
00:23:09,000 --> 00:23:12,000
His Double Machine Gun attack
shoots Nen bullets.

449
00:23:12,000 --> 00:23:14,000
Use your fingers as guns
for an extra punch!

450
00:23:15,000 --> 00:23:16,000
Pew, pew, pew!

451
00:23:22,000 --> 00:23:24,000
[Gon] Next time:
"A x Brutal x Battlefield."

452
00:23:25,000 --> 00:23:26,000
-Out.
-[Killua] Out?

453
00:23:26,000 --> 00:23:27,000
[Gon] Outfield!

454
00:23:27,000 --> 00:23:29,000
[Gon and Killua] Infield!
